tion" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/state.json" "file_sha256" "def1579efa9e17ed2eeb15ff956d4dffcaf647b3ec61664fe665a85b779303bf" "basis" 1238 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14035554/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-40291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $26{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-2}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n26{x}_{1}=26\\cdot \\frac{7}{13}=14.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-40291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-13"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 57\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+57\\cdot 7}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+399}{1+49} \\\\  & =\\frac{400}{50} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{1}}{2}=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-40401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $100{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}25 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 25+0\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-4)}{{25}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{25-12}{625+9+16} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{650} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n100{x}_{2}=100\\cdot \\frac{1}{50}=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-102352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102352" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $5{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot (-4)+(-4)\\cdot 2}{{(-4)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20-8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n5{x}_{1}=5\\cdot (-\\frac{7}{5})=-7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-102337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-28"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "17"] ["math" "30"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $15{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot (-3)}{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+12}{1+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n15{x}_{1}=15\\cdot \\frac{7}{5}=21.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json