q-81142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{6}}-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{6}{x}_{2}=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-81142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{6}"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]}$  of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{25}{\\sqrt{26}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}=-\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-40293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-40293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ -\\frac{24}{\\sqrt{26}}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]=\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]=1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-102322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}+1 \\\\ 1-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $5{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =x\\cdot {q}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4+0+3 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n5{x}_{2}=5\\cdot 7=35.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be4349c65571fc793709d8d1dd7eb4bea88395240d63b889474827188b99a91"} {"question" "q-102333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-35"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-102333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "35"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {"question" "q-81106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}=-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{10}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/state.json" "file_sha256" "d31ab2665898aaa953d3d4430f9486117308ffdb4ec4634ff080e05f01d75e7e"} {