fc05532528354b82231eab87ca49ec72bd42879759c64c4165837d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/example-7113.json" "file_sha256" "e480083cb61685c04b42a4df022e4643a5a51bf2d21bfb232e46831c47773095"} {"question" "e-7113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/1ba0b151abea3c5b1a050c6ff924f3718fcb045b063b1b47df7a73f9d15316c9.png) where $x_i = \\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i.$ Computing the components of $\\mathbf{x},$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-2-6=-8 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-4+3=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/51184680e9ec8b56a437334ca2a9281b1b364da2c35922839be13e545d92cec4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/example-7113.json" "file_sha256" "e480083cb61685c04b42a4df022e4643a5a51bf2d21bfb232e46831c47773095"}] "usage" {"e-7113" [] "q-81106" [] "e-7112" [] "q-40291" []} "basis" 2303 "retractions" [[17592186157710 :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of $R^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $26x_{1}$, where $x_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}$.\n\n$B = {\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 27\\end{bmatrix}}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186157013 :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ below, find the value of $x_2$, the second component of $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$.\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186157013 :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2,\\,\\mathbf{q}_3$.\n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ where\n\n$$\nx_i = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}{\\mathbf{q}_i \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}\n$$\n\nComputing $x_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{2} &= \\frac{x \\cdot q_{2}}{q_{2} \\cdot q_{2}} \\\\\n&= (4 \\cdot 1 + 6 \\cdot 1 + (-2) \\cdot (-4))/(1^{2} + 1^{2} + (-4)^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{4 + 6 + 8}{1 + 1 + 16} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186157014 :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ of $\\mathbb R^2$, find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ if $\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186157014 :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2$.\n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ where\n\n$$\nx_i = \\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i\n$$\n\nComputing the components of $\\mathbf{x}$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} =-2 - 6 =-8 \\\\\nx_{2} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} =-4 + 3 =-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186155513 17592186155514 17592186155515 17592186155516 17592186155517 17592186294809 17592186294810 17592186294811 17592186294812 17592186294813] "immutable_fields" [[17592186155512 :answer-field/correct] [17592186155512 :answer-field/id] [17592186155512 :answer-field/key] [17592186155512 :answer-field/type] [17592186294808 :answer-field/correct] [17592186294808 :answer-field/id] [17592186294808 :answer-field/key] [17592186294808 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
